{
  "name": "gap_anchor_topk_pairs",
  "intuition": "Build stable preferences by first filtering for clear objective wins via a configurable gap_threshold, then controlling pair count by anchoring comparisons on the best (lowest-objective) candidates per instance and pairing them only against sufficiently worse candidates; this reduces noisy near-ties and avoids quadratic explosion while keeping strong signal coverage.",
